      "id": "gallows-bell",
      "style": "standoff",
      "note": "Four bars of gallows air before anything hits: men's choir on bare fifths, the tolling bell, a whipcrack rim and a shaker. F#m–F#m–D–C# states the key and hangs on the harmonic-minor V, and the last two beats fire the canter up into the charge. Western on purpose — this is the only place in the piece with room in it.",
